STUDY SESSION

1.. Joint Citizen Participation Advisory Board (CPAB) Study Session with City Council

Roll Call of the Citizen Participation Advisory Board:  Peter Andres,  Shelly Grace-Bowers, Chris Byrne, Shayna Lathus, Mike Massie, Dr. Paul Morrow, Donna Traversi  -  Action: agenda title only {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Present: Peter Andres,  Shelly Grace-Bowers, Chris Byrne, and Shayna Lathus\par
Absent: Mike Massie, Dr. Paul Morrow, and Donna Traversi\par
\par
Deputy Director of Economic Development Kellee Fritzal and Shelly Grace-Bowers jointly presented a PowerPoint communication entitled: Citizen Participation Advisory Board (CPAB) 2019-20 Recommendations with slides titled: Estimated HUD Allocations 2019-20, CDBG Allocation Process, 2019-20 CPAB Recommendations, Public Services: 15% Cap(2), Admin, Housing &amp; Code Enforcement, Public Improvements, 2019/20 HOME Program, 2019/20 HOME Projects, Next Steps, and Questions.\par
\par
Councilmember Delgleize confirmed with Director Fritzal that code enforcement has the same allocation as last year.\par
\par
Councilmember Posey and staff discussed that a report and presentation by Stand up for Kids resulted in their award being doubled this year based on their success last year. \par
\par
Semeta - has issue reduction Homeless Outreach to PD/reason.  They took a little bit from everybody - to make stretch more.  Would like to see same allocation as last year to this group - Brenden concurred with Semeta on this issue\par
\par
Brenden - Admin housing/code enforcement - doesn't see last years/request amount same as last year.  HOME projects - what are uses? Fritzal: working with HUD how to utilize funds, transitional housing. Administration costs: staff time, consultants & monitoring/audits\par
\par
Carr - emphasized funds are not set at this time (estimates).  Section 108 loan -  this is last year to make payment - more funds will be available next year.  \par
\par
Hardy - agrees with MPT Semeta & Brenda re: allocation.\par
\par
Peterson - concurs, feels Police should be fully funded \par
\par
Posey - spoke to homeless issue and importance of working with homeless youth/ Peterson concurred\par
\par
Posey/Semeta motioned to recess to Closed Session\par
}


